# Reggie James

> Reggie James is a UK go-to-market and growth adviser to B2B technology leaders and the investors who back them, based in Guildford, Surrey, and London. His line: "The right decisions change everything. I help tech leaders make the ones that grow their business."

He brings 25 years of building, scaling and selling technology businesses: founding Digital Clarity in 2002, building DC Storm through to its acquisition by Rakuten, leading commercial operations for an internet business listed in Singapore, and serving since 2011 as COO and Executive Director of DBMM Group Inc. (OTC: DBMM), the US public company that owns Digital Clarity.

## Who he works with

- Founders, CEOs and leadership teams of B2B technology companies between value proposition and exit.
- VC, private equity and private investors backing B2B technology.

## What clients get

- Go-to-market strategy: segment priorities, positioning, pricing, sales motion and a growth accelerator programme.
- Marketing that builds pipeline: messaging, demand model, channels, AI search visibility and board reporting.
- Execution and commercial leadership: hands-on leadership of sales and marketing, monthly or fractional.
- For investors: commercial due diligence, a portfolio accelerator for companies behind plan, and portfolio go-to-market reviews.

Most clients start with a discovery call and a go-to-market review. Digital Clarity, his firm, delivers programmes when a team is needed.

## Key facts

- Founder and Managing Director, Digital Clarity (since 2002). Grew it to 25 to 30 people and more than 200 clients, including Adobe, Xerox and Bentley Systems.
- Built DC Storm, a marketing measurement platform used by around 48% of major media planning and buying agencies before its acquisition by Rakuten.
- COO, Senior Vice President and Executive Director, DBMM Group Inc. (OTC: DBMM), since 2011.
- Earlier: AltaVista global sales; a senior commercial role at a Singapore internet business that listed on SIMEX and was acquired; technology publishing at VNU and Ziff Davis.
- Selected client results: software ARR from $8m to $23m in three years; 88% EMEA revenue growth in 12 months with a 37.6% lower cost per acquisition; 30% more qualified demo requests year on year.
- Host of the Reggie James - Perspectives podcast.

